      "message": "I believe it should be safe to use pAnnot instead of calling GetFocusAnnot() again, which is guaranteed to return the exact same pointer as pAnnot in this case.\n\nHowever I did not make that change because there\u0027s a possibility that if we used pAnnot then it could be changed to null after calling GetNextAnnot(), then the pNext.Get() !\u003d pFocusAnnot would potentially compare against null, which would always trigger the if statement.\n\nIt\u0027s not clear to me if this logical possibility is a case that we need to maintain the current behavior for.",
